    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0781" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg761"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Lord
                        Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 4, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Referring to Mr. Burnley’s
                    communication of the 7th ultimo, relative to the refusal of the collector of the
                    port of New York to grant a clearance of certain merchandise shipped by Messrs.
                    Darrell &amp; Nash to Nassau, in the Bahama islands, I have the honor, in reply,
                    to enclose for your lordship’s information a copy of a letter of the 29th ultimo
                    from the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, my lord, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d556-a1.xml" xpointer="d556-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
